{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/955336-running-my-first-game-tips-and-tricks-wanted","id":955336,"title":"Running my first game; Tips and Tricks wanted","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-21T18:09:34-07:00","id":955336,"title":"Running my first game; Tips and Tricks wanted","content":"Hello again,<br /> So I convinced some family to play a short chronicle with me. I'll be a storyteller since I have the books and they've never played the game before. I've been reading the Storyteller's handbook (1st edition only so far), the Storyteller's Companion (will be using the 2ed screen), the W20 corebook, the 2ed corebook, and the introductory kit. I got some good ideas from those resources, but I would also like to hear some advice from the veterans out there.<br /> Thanks a bunch!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12036-story","name":"Story","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T19:29:24-07:00","id":955362,"title":"","content":"This initially won't terribly helpful. Apologies.<br /> <br /> Can you be any more specific in what sort of advice you are looking for?<br /> How many players do you have? Any idea on what tribes they're going to play? Auspices? Where is the game set? Anything you know already can be helpful.<br /> <br /> Best I can think of without any additional information is to keep the beginning stories small in scope. Make them personal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T20:13:42-07:00","id":955380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/955336-running-my-first-game-tips-and-tricks-wanted?p=955362#post955362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This initially won't terribly helpful. Apologies.<br /> <br /> Can you be any more specific in what sort of advice you are looking for?<br /> How many players do you have? Any idea on what tribes they're going to play? Auspices? Where is the game set? Anything you know already can be helpful.<br /> <br /> Best I can think of without any additional information is to keep the beginning stories small in scope. Make them personal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I should have been more specific, sorry about that.<br /> <br /> I'm looking for any advice to give, either on the mechanics, how to be a good ST, how to keep players engaged, how much combat/character building should be in a given session, how &quot;lore heavy&quot; I should be ect. Although specfically I want to know more about enemy creation and how many NPC creation since that's what I'm struggling the most with at the moment.<br /> <br /> The game will be on my birthday and I'm planning on it lasting 4 hours or so (shorter or longer depending on what the players do). It will be standalone, but I would love to continue it with them if they have fun.<br /> I have two players ages 16 and 9; the youngest seems the most interested. I plan on making a Rite of Passage chronicle since they aren't too familiar with the WOD or anything roleplaying related in general. It be set in New York state in 1999 (the year the old Rage Across New York was published, which I'm also heavily referencing). The players are a Silver Fang homid Ragabash (the 16 year old) and a Shadow Lord homid Ahroun (the 9 year old) who are both cubs and, having recently experienced their first change outside of their tribes and have become fosterlings for a group of Children of Gaia near Finger Lakes. They are joined by a third pack member, a Gaian Metis Philodox cub that I made up to help answer their questions while staying in character.<br /> <br /> The goal of the chronicle is for the players is not only become cliath by the end, but also discover their deed names and their pack names, have a better understanding of Garou society (and WTA in general), and reconcile their characters' grievences with their respective parents.<br /> In the session they will battle a fomori, a few banes, maybe duel each other?, and have a black spiral dancer boss whom I plan on running away or escaping in the end.<br /> <br /> That's really all I have so far except for a few NPC ideas and some plot beats for the chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12036-story","user":"Story","date":". 08-21-2016, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12036-story","name":"Story","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T20:42:31-07:00","id":955388,"title":"","content":"First time Storyteller with a group of new players... I don't envy you because that can be daunting.<br /> <br /> Well I'd first recommend getting your hands on some pre-made adventures for WtA (or for the WoD/CofD in general) to see things can be laid out in adventures if not out right use for your game. Unfortunately I'm not too aware of many WtA pre-made adventures that would be suitable. There is W20 Skinner but its not really suited for entry level PCs and giving players the extra XP to be at that level could be problematic to new players. There is Rite of Passage which would work wonders for them as it revolves around a pack of young Garou sent on their Rite of Passage when things go wrong. Unfortunately it is a first edition book which means is dated in mechanics and some of the setting and a bit on the wonky side compared to what WtA is now. But if you have the time, you can rework the dated and wonkier scenes into something bit more modern and update the NPC stats.<br /> <br /> Second you may want to consider creating Player/Storyteller Rule Books. What that is taking the pages on the various rules and mechanics, copying them and putting it into a binder with dividers to organize them. This works best if you have the PDF copies of the books as its just some simple print jobs rather than photocopying physical books. It's a thing that I've seen many times and I've started to get into it myself. It is much easier to sort through a single book than a dozen.<br /> <br /> And of course you can continue using the book beyond this game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T20:57:41-07:00","id":955397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/955336-running-my-first-game-tips-and-tricks-wanted?p=955388#post955388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First time Storyteller with a group of new players... I don't envy you because that can be daunting.<br /> <br /> Well I'd first recommend getting your hands on some pre-made adventures for WtA (or for the WoD/CofD in general) to see things can be laid out in adventures if not out right use for your game. Unfortunately I'm not too aware of many WtA pre-made adventures that would be suitable. There is W20 Skinner but its not really suited for entry level PCs and giving players the extra XP to be at that level could be problematic to new players. There is Rite of Passage which would work wonders for them as it revolves around a pack of young Garou sent on their Rite of Passage when things go wrong. Unfortunately it is a first edition book which means is dated in mechanics and some of the setting and a bit on the wonky side compared to what WtA is now. But if you have the time, you can rework the dated and wonkier scenes into something bit more modern and update the NPC stats.<br /> <br /> Second you may want to consider creating Player/Storyteller Rule Books. What that is taking the pages on the various rules and mechanics, copying them and putting it into a binder with dividers to organize them. This works best if you have the PDF copies of the books as its just some simple print jobs rather than photocopying physical books. It's a thing that I've seen many times and I've started to get into it myself. It is much easier to sort through a single book than a dozen.<br /> <br /> And of course you can continue using the book beyond this game.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I just bought Rite of Passage on Amazon and I planned on looking through it. I was worried about the old mechanics too, but then again I'm also referencing Rage Across New York (though mostly just to get a feel of the garou and spirit culture and demographics there). I'm kinda just trying to see what works and what doesn't based on the core rule books I'm using Revised and W20.<br /> <br /> Creating Player/Storyteller Rule Books is a really, really good idea! I'm already typing their starting gifts and rules at the moment but they might also get confused over the simple mechanics as well. I'm trying to brake out of character as little as possible and I am worried that too much mechanic explaintion would slow the game down and bore them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12036-story","name":"Story","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T21:41:55-07:00","id":955419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/955336-running-my-first-game-tips-and-tricks-wanted?p=955380#post955380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah I should have been more specific, sorry about that.<br /> <br /> I'm looking for any advice to give, either on the mechanics, how to be a good ST, how to keep players engaged, how much combat/character building should be in a given session, how &quot;lore heavy&quot; I should be ect. Although specfically I want to know more about enemy creation and how many NPC creation since that's what I'm struggling the most with at the moment.<br /> <br /> The game will be on my birthday and I'm planning on it lasting 4 hours or so (shorter or longer depending on what the players do). It will be standalone, but I would love to continue it with them if they have fun.<br /> I have two players ages 16 and 9; the youngest seems the most interested. I plan on making a Rite of Passage chronicle since they aren't too familiar with the WOD or anything roleplaying related in general. It be set in New York state in 1999 (the year the old Rage Across New York was published, which I'm also heavily referencing). The players are a Silver Fang homid Ragabash (the 16 year old) and a Shadow Lord homid Ahroun (the 9 year old) who are both cubs and, having recently experienced their first change outside of their tribes and have become fosterlings for a group of Children of Gaia near Finger Lakes. They are joined by a third pack member, a Gaian Metis Philodox cub that I made up to help answer their questions while staying in character.<br /> <br /> The goal of the chronicle is for the players is not only become cliath by the end, but also discover their deed names and their pack names, have a better understanding of Garou society (and WTA in general), and reconcile their characters' grievences with their respective parents.<br /> In the session they will battle a fomori, a few banes, maybe duel each other?, and have a black spiral dancer boss whom I plan on running away or escaping in the end.<br /> <br /> That's really all I have so far except for a few NPC ideas and some plot beats for the chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. several thoughts on this. Any of the darker parts of the WoD should be skipped over, given the age of your players. Also be wary of the difficulty curve, since you have new players, and they're young and you have a small pack. For a starter session, I would (and have) just plan on running through the pack coming together, figuring out who is Alpha/Beta (the NPC shouldn't be either if you can help it) and a short-ish Rite of Passage. I wouldn't worry about being too lore heavy for the moment. Knowledge of Garou society comes from experience, which can be gained more in later sessions. Especially if they changed away from their tribes, it should be fine to skip over for the most part (for now).<br /> on this: &quot;In the session they will battle a fomori, a few banes, maybe duel each other?, and have a black spiral dancer boss whom I plan on running away or escaping in the end.&quot;<br /> a few banes can be overwhelming easily, unless they're extremely weak. What is the story hook for getting them involved in these fights? And I wouldn't use a BSD unless your dead set on it. Spirals are exactly as powerful as the PCs. This one is going to be at least slightly more so since it's going to be a rank or 2 higher I would guess. Things could go south very quickly messing with Spirals. Banes too really.<br /> <br /> So I would jot down a quick outline of events you have planned to get them started.<br /> 1. PCs meet.<br /> 2. Leadership challenge (this is where you'll get a duel or gamecraft)<br /> 3. Caern interactions (meeting some Elder).<br /> 4. sent on Rite of Passage.<br /> 5. your story plans<br /> 6. Return to caern, get names and rank<br /> <br /> <br /> And for rules, just familiarize yourself with the basics for now. Take <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar420_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"420\" data-vbnamecard=\"420\">AkatsukiLeader13</a>'s advice and put together a cheat sheet. The screens help a lot for this if you want to use them.<br /> <br /> Edit: afterthoughts: Don't worry about being overly serious if you don't want to be, given the player's ages.<br /> I once ran a Rite of Passage where the pack had to find a corrupted creature in the woods. They thought it was a fomori bear. It turned out to be a Vampire Rabbit (long story, doesn't matter). It was a 9th gen Bratovitch Tzimisce Hare in Horrid form that was using Bonecraft strikes against them. It was a serious fight off of a ridiculous premise. Later when the Vampire players realized they thought it was pretty funny. They had the pack coming together, with challenges to determine leaders, and then meeting the Ritesmaster and then the Rite of Passage, which had an investigation phase, and then a chase scene and then a boss fight. Filled out a session nicely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 08-22-2016, 12:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T21:47:24-07:00","id":955422,"title":"","content":"Read Rite of Passage if for no other reason than as an example. And if you are using Rage Across New York then Rite of Passage would still work as the PC pack is from New York, with the opening starting in New York with the pack being sent via Moonbridge to another Sept in Canada for their Rite of Passage.<br /> <br /> As for updating it, as I recall, much of the NPCs were of the generic verity, the kind that should be in the Antagonists section of W20. The rest shouldn't be too hard as most of the stats remained the same. It's more just some tweaking here and there.<br /> <br /> It's been a while since I've read my copy of RoP. I'll skim through it tomorrow and give a more proper assessment on what needs to be changed.<br /> <br /> As for the rules, just use W20. For novices, having bunch of books to go through is a bad thing. W20 has a wealth of material that in previous editions was spread over multiple books, including at least some of the books you mentioned in the first post. Like I said before, if you have W20 on PDF and a printer it will be easy to print out the pages on the game systems, rules and mechanics as well as the Gifts. With the Gifts you can make it a little easier for the players as you can print out just the pages with the Gifts the PCs have and cross out all the Gifts on those pages they don't have. You could even color code it by circling the Gifts the players have in two different colors, one for each player so they will be able to quickly reference their powers.<br /> <br /> I know you want to avoid confusion and pauses in play but with novices that's going to be difficult. They don't have experience with the game and its rules. They're going to be pausing to look things up or for you to explain something. Creating the rule book I talked about can help, especially if you have it properly sectioned off with labelled dividers can help to reduce it as it makes it easier for everyone to look things when needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T08:51:27-07:00","id":955619,"title":"","content":"So I just skimmed through RoP and it isn't as wonky as I thought. The only scene I'd drop, I would drop the optional scene in the second chapter that involves the Fae.<br /> <br /> All it really needs is some tweaking of NPC stats and much of that is already done for you in W20 as many of the encountered NPCs are the generic kind that have templates written up in W20. For the rest its just some readjusting of the Abilities as some in the 1E no longer exist, and changing some of the Gifts and other Powers that have been removed or otherwise changed.<br /> <br /> It's doable without too much work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T11:00:30-07:00","id":955709,"title":"","content":"If you are worried about getting bogged down with rules and dice rolls just make a lot of St calls. The nice thing about it being new for everyone at the table is that you all get to learn and enjoy the game together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T05:39:50-07:00","id":987207,"title":"","content":"I wanted to thank everyone for the response and tips. My players and myself really had a lot of fun. Even the 16 year old who really got into it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12036-story","name":"Story","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}